        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 12,
        "titulo": "Contractions and colloquial expressions",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: in fast, informal speech, words get SHORTER: «сейчас» becomes «щас», «здравствуйте» becomes «здрасте», «пожалуйста» is said [pa-ZHAL-sta], «сколько» sounds [SKOL-ka]. STEP 2: «ЧЕГО» takes the place of «почему» or «что»: «Ты чего не пришёл?» (why didn't you come?). STEP 3: «ДАВАЙ» and «ЛАДНО» are short replies: «Давай!» (let's / OK), «Ладно!» (fine). STEP 4: «НУ ТЫ ДАЁШЬ!» is an exclamation of astonishment (\"you're something else!\"). STEP 5: use these forms ONLY with friends; at work and in formal writing, use the full forms. STEP 6: intonation shows emotion: a question goes up, a statement goes down. English does the same with \"gonna\", \"wanna\" and \"y'all\"; they are fine among friends but not in a letter.",
